# Cosmolog API (Rust)

## Layout

```text
routes/   # thin HTTP handlers
domain/   # models, repositories, validation, presenters
auth/     # AuthUser, OptionalAuth, JWT
infra/    # db, migrate, aws, email, storage, logging
error.rs  # AppError → JSON { "error": ... }
```

## Patterns

1. Extract `AuthUser` or `OptionalAuth` → call domain → `Result<Json<T>, AppError>`.
2. Ownership checks in domain/routes — privileged DB role; no RLS reliance.
3. Image URLs: `domain/url_validation.rs`.
4. Status: `401` unauthorized (often instead of 403), `404`, `400`, `409` unique.

## Migrations

```bash
cd apps/api && sqlx migrate add describe_your_change
# edit migrations/<ts>_describe_your_change.sql
```

Never write new SQL under `supabase/migrations/`.

## Tests

Add coverage in `apps/api/tests/` (`api_*.rs`, `repositories_*.rs`) using `tests/common/`. Run with `TEST_DATABASE_URL` + `docker-compose.test.yml`.
